NAME
       browse - a tiny text-only web browser (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       browse [-b "name=value"] [-d "field=value&..."] URL

DESCRIPTION
       browse fetches a page and shows it the way a person would see it in a
       browser: the words on the page, its links numbered [1], [2]... (listed
       at the end with where they go) and its forms with the names of their
       fields. That makes a page easy to read and shows you which fields a
       form sends.

       Like a real browser, browse does not show the hidden parts of a page:
       comments (<!-- ... -->), scripts and hidden settings. To see those, look
       at the page's source with curl.

       browse is a Cyber Range practice tool; it only reaches the range's
       pretend web servers.

OPTIONS
       -b "name=value"
              Send a cookie (as curl -b does), for example a session cookie
              from signing in.

       -d "field=value&..."
              Send form fields with the request (as curl -d does).

EXAMPLES
           browse http://copperleaf.example/
           browse -b "session=s1234..." http://copperleaf.example/account

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), webscan(1)
